  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6c0z41",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3871974930,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Account/Mutations/CreateUnder18AccountMutation.cs",
      "line": 43,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3871974930",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "This error message is used both when `DateOfBirth` is invalid/unparseable and when the child is 18+. When parsing fails, returning “The child must be under 18.” is misleading for clients and makes bad-input troubleshooting harder. Split the parse validation from the age check so the message matches the actual failure.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Split date parsing from the under-18 eligibility check so malformed dates return a specific validation message, and added regression coverage for the malformed-date response."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eACIA",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3901559412,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Account/Services/EnrolmentProvider.cs",
      "line": 85,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3901559412",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "The comment says the Identity endpoint may create an enabled \"verified-email\" identity, but the new `RegisterUnder18` endpoint forces `AccountEnabled=false` and `SuppressCommunication=true`. Please update the comment to reflect the actual (dummy-email managed-child) behavior so future changes don’t assume a supported verified-email path here.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Updated the comment to describe the actual RegisterUnder18 contract: a disabled, communication-suppressed managed-child identity using the generated dummy email."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eACIT",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3901559445,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Account/Services/EnrolmentProvider.cs",
      "line": 99,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3901559445",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`EnrolUnder18Member` throws `InvalidOperationException` for missing enrolment identifiers and Identity registration failures. That produces an unstructured GraphQL error (no controlled `extensions.code`) and can bypass the mutation’s controlled error envelope. Align this with the existing `EnrolFcMember` behavior by throwing `GraphQLException` with a code/source so clients get deterministic failures.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Replaced both InvalidOperationException paths with structured GraphQLException errors carrying deterministic code, message, and source fields, consistent with the existing enrolment provider convention."
    }
  ],
